{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 ends in TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received with tohost FAIL 0xdead, so recv_buf_valid never asserted. In state 10 the receiver should set recv_buf_valid to 1 when recv_divcnt exceeds cfg_divider, but picosoc/simpleuart.v:92 drives recv_buf_valid <= 2 which truncates to 0 for a 1-bit flag. This single wrong constant explains the timeout; CONE_SLICE has no simpleuart provenance only picosoc/spiflash.v and scripts/quartus/system.v refs so trace plus excerpt govern.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@
 				10: begin
 					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
-						recv_buf_valid <= 2;
+						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS with uart byte 0xa5 received, no TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received"}

